1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,980
Welcome to the Architectural Matrix
Demonstrator.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:11,080
In the previous scenarios, we saw why
naive, schema-free graphs collapse when

3
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:14,380
confronted with time, history, and
engineering rules.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,760
Once an organization accepts that it needs
formal semantics, the engineering

5
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:24,100
leadership immediately faces a two-by-two
architectural crossroads.

6
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:31,560
On the horizontal axis, you must choose
your top-level ontological commitment at

7
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:33,220
the SMIM layer.

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:40,900
Do you model the world in three dimensions
using BFO, the Basic Formal Ontology,

9
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:45,120
where physical parts are enduring objects
that pass through time?

10
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:52,620
Or do you model the world in four
dimensions using ISO 15926, where every

11
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:58,120
physical object is a spatiotemporal worm
sliced into immutable historical states?

12
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:06,020
On the vertical axis, you must choose your
physical graph storage mechanism at the SMS layer.

13
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:11,247
Do you deploy a labeled property graph, LPG, 

14
00:01:11,247 --> 00:01:15,260
where nodes and edges carry internal
key-value dictionaries?

15
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:22,380
Or do you deploy a W3C Resource
Description Framework store, RDF, where

16
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:27,940
